course: dictionary
lesson: 3132
title: Eleven in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Eleven is a number, but it can also name a team. Look at the words around it to know which meaning fits. «Zara kept a game diary and was shocked: eleven hours of games that week and forty minutes of reading.» Here eleven is a number of hours, so it means 11.
explain: «A team of eleven players» is different. The word team tells you that eleven is a group, not a count of hours. Football and cricket teams have eleven players, so a team of eleven is called an eleven.
explain: Numbers in a story can carry a big idea. «The Magician» gives back Pau Amma's hard shell «for eleven months of the year». The number tells you that the deal is mostly fair, but the twelfth month is the catch.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If you read «eleven hours of games» and swap in «the number 11 of hours», it still makes sense. That is how you know you have it right.
fact: Eleven is the number 11, one more than ten.
fact: A team of eleven players is called an eleven, as in football and cricket.
fact: 11 is a prime number, because only 1 and 11 divide into it exactly.
fact: 11 × 11 = 121.
fact: «Eleven o'clock» is a time of day, and it means 11 on the clock.
exercise: Find the number that is one more than ten. | *Eleven | Twelve | Ten | Nine
exercise: «The Magician» gives Pau Amma his shell back «for eleven months of the year». How many months is that? | *Eleven | Twelve | Six | Ten
exercise: Zara spent «eleven hours of games» that week. What does eleven mean here? | *The number 11 | A kind of game | A team of players | A time of day
test: «The Islamic calendar is about eleven days shorter than the sun's year.» What does eleven tell us? | A number of days | A type of moon | *A number of days, 11, shorter than the sun's year | The name of a month
test: Which of these is 11 × 11? | *121 | 111 | 22 | 110
exam: Which of these is a prime number? | Twelve | Nine | *Eleven | Ten
